248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (A 54-year-old university professor has become an unexpected celebrity among young people in China. Professor Biao Xiang is not a pop star or an actor. He is an anthropologist who studies society and social change. However, thousands of young people are now following his talks and treating him almost like an idol.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (The reason for his popularity is simple: he talks openly about anxiety and the pressure young people have. China has developed very quickly, but this has also created a lot of competition. Young people worry about finding a good job, having a good career, relationships and being able to afford a home.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (The transition from school to working life can be especially difficult. Many people feel that they must get a good degree, find a secure job, get married and buy a house. Because so many people are competing for the same things, they can feel exhausted and worried about not being successful.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (Professor Xiang believes that people often depend too much on exams, jobs and other systems to decide how successful they are. Instead, he encourages young people to understand themselves and find meaning in their relationships with others.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (For many of his young fans, Xiang is important because he makes them feel understood. His unusual popularity shows how much young people want someone to talk honestly about their worries and fears.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
